THE SOURCES BEHIND THE FIGURES
===================================================================

Feeding at Bethesda (source-material/40-feeding-numbers.md), October 2026,
which rests on Bethesda's own account of what it buys and on Lagos and
national market prices found online in October 2026. Each price source is
cited inside that document.

How blind Nigerians earn a living (source-material/41-how-blind-nigerians-
earn-a-living.md), October 2026, which rests on published, peer-reviewed
studies and national surveys, each cited inside that document with its
link and the date it was read.

Reading SUN (reading-sun.html and the sun/ folder): derived from the SUN
New Testament PDF published with Wycliffe Associates' permission, the
Epistle of James SUN resource from Bible Translation Tools, and the
English Unlocked Literal Bible, all Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
4.0. The files in sun/ are published under that same licence, CC BY-SA 4.0,
not CC BY. The glosses are our statistical inference and are not confirmed
by Wycliffe Associates. Working papers: source-material/36, 38 and 39.

Headcounts: a visit by our representative on 24 October 2026, and
Bethesda's letters.

The Nigeria National Blindness and Visual Impairment Survey (2005 to 2007)
is the starting point for the future studies on why people are blind in
Nigeria; it will be cited on those pages when they are written.

WHAT IS NEVER HERE
===================================================================

Bank, transfer or account details of anyone. The pay of anyone who works
with us. The names, pictures or stories of students or individuals in
Nigeria without their documented consent. Private assessments of partner
organizations.

HOW TO CITE
===================================================================

  Brian Clark, "Blind in Nigeria" (working name),
  https://1eyebiney.github.io/blind-in-nigeria/, accessed <date>.

For a particular page, add its title and address. For the ledger as data,
cite data/ledger.json in this repository and the date you took it.

Attribution is the only thing CC BY asks for, and it is what lets a reader
trace a claim back to its source. Please keep it.
